# CH06 — The Bell That Broke. Drowned Archive, Rook, the Bell-Sworn Custodian.

@scene D05_ENTER once
say narr | The tide door stands open at low water. Salt light moves across drowned shelves.
say pip | Records nobody owns. Contracts older than the Crown. The ministry forgot this place because it couldn't tax it.
say oriel | Three bells on the nave floor. Old archives opened by tone.
objective pip | Open the Bell Nave's galleries by matching bell tones to their doors.
@end

@scene D05_BELL_LOW
sfx FX031
setvar d05_tone 1
say narr | A low tone rolls through the nave. (ANCHOR glyph.) The west door hums.
@end

@scene D05_BELL_MID
sfx FX031
setvar d05_tone 2
say narr | A middle tone, clear as water. (WAVE glyph.) The east door hums.
@end

@scene D05_BELL_HIGH
sfx FX031
setvar d05_tone 3
say narr | A high tone rings bright. (LANTERN glyph.) Somewhere deeper, past the dry gallery, a door answers.
@end

@scene D05_DOOR_DRY
if var:d05_tone==1 open
say narr | The anchor door stays shut. (It answers to the low tone - ring the west bell.)
end
label open
sfx FX009
set d05_dry
say narr | The anchor door slides back into the wall.
@end

@scene D05_DOOR_WET
if var:d05_tone==2 open
say narr | The wave door stays shut. (It answers to the middle tone - ring the north bell.)
end
label open
sfx FX009
set d05_wet
say narr | The wave door lifts, and seawater sighs in over the threshold.
@end

@scene D05_DOOR_VAULT
if var:d05_tone==3 open
say narr | The lantern door stays shut. (It answers to the high tone - the east bell in the nave.)
end
label open
sfx FX009
set d05_vault
say narr | The lantern door opens onto the Witness Vault.
@end

@scene D05_CUSTODIAN once
music silence
say narr | A figure of salt and bronze rises from the vault floor. Three bells hang from its shoulders.
say "Custodian" | UNREGISTERED READERS. THE ARCHIVE IS SEALED.
say pip | Registered, unregistered. Everyone always wants a form.
say oriel | When one bell vibrates, it mirrors the last element used. Change elements - or use steel.
battle B05 noflee
set b05_done
music M023
say narr | The Custodian settles back into the floor, its bells silent. The shelves around the vault stay open.
show rook 20 26 up rook
move rook up up up up
say rook | Don't close it again. Please. I've been trying to reach this vault for two years.
say dain | Who are you?
say rook | Elian Rook. Ministry geologist, until I wrote the wrong report. I study heartglass.
say rook | The organs are not fossils. They are transmitting. Continuously. A distributed consciousness spread across every relay in the kingdom.
say rook | I don't ask you to believe me. I have names, dates, and the transmission logs. Read them.
xp 200
key K_ROOK_EVIDENCE
doc Rook's_Evidence | Relay transmission logs, 312 years of samples. The pulse is not random: it repeats, it answers, it forms patterns that change when names are spoken near it. Extraction increases output and suffering-analogous distortion together. Appendix: seven relay sites. Appendix page 9 missing.
say tessa | Page nine is missing.
say rook | Water damage.
say nera | The pages on either side are dry.
say rook | ...Water damage.
objective | Speak with Rook in the Witness Vault.
@end

@scene D05_ROOK_TALK
say rook | There is a last synchronization chamber, under the Crown Dais in Veyr. If the relays could be released from there -
say dain | We investigate. Nothing more until we understand it.
say rook | Investigate. Yes. Of course.
say narr | The Roof Pier is north of the vault.
@end

@scene CH06_ROOF once
say narr | The roof pier. The tide is turning. From the harbor, a bell rings - a real bell, rehung by the town.
say pip | They're copying the evidence. Every family in Bellharbor is taking a page home.
say rook | You can't burn a thousand copies.
say oriel | You can ignore them.
say rook | Not if we act.
say dain | We're going to see the chamber. That's all.
say narr | Rook agrees quickly. Too quickly, Nera thinks. She doesn't say so yet.
say narr | Something long and gentle rises under the pier: a serpent-shaped Vestige, humming the harbor bell's note.
say whale | You rang the old bells and did not seal the doors again. I will answer your call.
vestige V03
chapter CH06
set rook_ally
say rook | The Pale Basin holds the memory vaults. That's where the relays remember what they were. The route north is the Skychain.
objective rook | Take the coastal ferry north to Skyspine (east pier on the world road), then the Skychain Viaduct.
discover L_D06
rumor | Sailors say the Skychain's anchors failed; High Aerie is sending a volunteer to reset them alone.
level_floor 13
warp WORLD ferry_bh left
@end
